["Here is a basic structure for your ClinicStatusUpdater service in PHP, without including all the specific details about how to connect to databases or other APIs. Please note that this example needs additional work to handle edge cases, integrate into an existing system, and provide robustness against issues like timeouts and failed updates:

```php
<?php
namespace Clinic;

use Clinic\DatabaseInterface;
use Clinic\APIClientInterface;
use Psr\Log\LoggerInterface;

class ClinicStatusUpdater {
    private $dbClient;
    private $apiClient;
    private $logger;

    public function __construct(DatabaseInterface $db, APIClientInterface $api, LoggerInterface $logger) {
        $this->dbClient = $db;
        $this->apiClient = $api;
        $this->logger = $logger;
    }

    public function updateStatusAsync(array $clinicIds, string $newStatus, string $lastModifiedIP): void {
        foreach ($clinicIds as $id) {
            $result = $this->apiClient->updateClinicStatusAsync($id, $newStatus);
            if ($result === false) {
                $this->logger->error('Failed to update clinic status in API: ' . $id);
                continue; // or throw an exception based on your requirement
            }
        }
    }

    public function updateStatus(array $clinicIds, string $newStatus, string $lastModifiedIP): void {
        $this->dbClient->startTransaction();
        foreach ($clinicIds as $id) {
            $result = $this->apiClient->updateClinicStatus($id, $newStatus);
            if ($result === false) {
                $this->logger->error('Failed to update clinic status in API: ' . $id);
                $this->dbClient->rollbackTransaction();
                return; // or throw an exception based on your requirement
            }
            $this->dbClient->updateClinicStatus($id, $newStatus, $lastModifiedIP);
        }
        $this->dbClient->commitTransaction();
    }

    public function healthCheck(): bool {
        return $this->apiClient->ping() && $this->dbClient->isConnected();
    }
}
?>
```

This service is using interfaces for database and API clients, which allows you to use any class implementing those interfaces. This makes it easy to replace the actual implementation with a mock in your tests or a real one when running in production.

The updateStatusAsync method updates statuses asynchronously by calling `updateClinicStatusAsync` on each clinic ID, logging an error if it fails. The updateStatus method updates all statuses synchronously and uses transactions to ensure data consistency, rolling back changes if any update fails. 

Finally, the healthCheck method checks that both API and database clients are connected properly.
