    cv.wait(lock, []{ return ready == true; });

    // Process the data here
    // ...

    // Once processed, mark the data as not ready and notify all waiting threads
    ready = false;
    cv.notify_all();
}

int main() {
    std::thread t1(fetchDataFromRepo);
    std::thread t2(processData);

    t1.join();
    t2.join();

    return 0;
}
```
In this basic setup, there are two threads: one for fetching the data from an external repository (`fetchDataFromRepo`), and another for processing that data (`processData`). The `ready` flag is used to signal when new data has been fetched and is ready to be processed. 

