['Here is a basic implementation based on your requirements using Spring Boot for the service, Lombok for boilerplate code reduction, Jackson for JSON serialization/deserialization, Apache HttpClient for HTTP requests to third-party APIs, Caffeine for caching and Guava for rate limiting. Note that this is a simplified solution and many details such as logging configuration or exception handling should be tailored according to your specific needs:

```java
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;
import lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;
import org.apache.http.HttpEntity;
import org.apache.http.client.methods.CloseableHttpResponse;
import org.apache.http.client.methods.HttpGet;
import org.apache.http.impl.client.CloseableHttpClient;
import org.apache.http.util.EntityUtils;
import com.github.benmanes.caffeine.cache.Caffeine;
import com.google.common.util.concurrent.RateLimiter;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Value;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.time.Duration;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;

@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Service
public class UserActivityService {
    private final ObjectMapper objectMapper;
    private final CloseableHttpClient httpclient;
    private final Caffeine<Object, Object> caffeineCache = Caffeine.newBuilder()
            .maximumSize(10_000)
            .expireAfterWrite(1, TimeUnit.HOURS)
            .build();

    @Value("${externalAPI.url}")
    private String externalAPIUrl;

    private final RateLimiter rateLimiter = RateLimiter.create(20); // 20 requests per second

    public String getUserActivityStats(User user) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        if (rateLimiter.tryAcquire()) {
            HashMap<String, Object> cachedResponse = caffeineCache.getIfPresent(user.getId());
            if (cachedResponse != null) return objectMapper.writeValueAsString(cachedResponse);

            HttpGet request = new HttpGet(externalAPIUrl + user.getId());
            try (CloseableHttpResponse response = httpclient.execute(request)) {
                HttpEntity entity = response.getEntity();
                String apiResult = EntityUtils.toString(entity);

                HashMap<String, Object> parsedApiResult = objectMapper.readValue(apiResult, HashMap.class);
                caffeineCache.put(user.getId(), parsedApiResult);

                return objectMapper.writeValueAsString(parsedApiResult);
            }
        } else {
            Thread.sleep(Duration.ofSeconds(1).toMillis()); // Wait for the next rate limit window
            getUserActivityStats(user);
        }

        return null;
    }
}
```

Please adapt this code according to your specific needs and add missing parts like User model, error handling, integration tests etc. 

Note: The above solution assumes you have a Spring Boot project set up. If not, please refer to the appropriate documentation on how to setup Spring Boot applications. Also note that in production-grade applications, some aspects such as logging or exception handling would need more attention and customization. Always remember to carefully handle sensitive data like API keys or user information to ensure security.
']

