['This task involves designing a complete JavaScript framework from scratch which isn't possible in this text-based format as it requires extensive coding and configuration files to be set up properly. But I can provide a high-level overview using modern web development best practices, considering each of your requirements.

```javascript
class Loader {
    constructor() {
        this.cache = {};
    }

    async load(url) {
        if (!this.cache[url]) {
            const res = await fetch(url); //fetch from API endpoint

            if (res.ok) { 
                const code = await res.text();
                this.cache[url] = new Function('', code); // Create a function to execute component.
            } else {
                throw new Error("Couldn't load component.");
            }
        }

        return this.cache[url];
    }
}

class Executor {
    constructor() {
        this.loader = new Loador();
        this.queue = [];
    }

    async run(component) {
        if (this.queue.includes(component)) return; // Avoid duplicate execution of components.

        const dependencies = component.dependencies || [];

        for (let dep of dependencies) { 
            await this.run(dep); 
        }

        try {
            const fn = await this.loader.load(component.url);
            fn(); // Execute the loaded function.
        } catch (e) {
            console.error('Error executing component:', e);
        }

        this.queue.push(component);
    }
}
```
This code provides a base on which you could expand upon to create your framework. 
- A `Loader` class handles fetching and caching of components asynchronously.
- An `Executor` class manages the order of execution, ensuring dependent components are loaded before they're executed.

Remember, this is only a basic implementation for understanding purposes. It lacks error handling, logging, user configuration interfaces etc. A complete solution would need much more detailed planning and design. You might want to use existing libraries like Webpack or Parcel if you're looking to implement such a system in production. 

Also, it’s important to note that running remote code can pose significant security risks, so make sure your API endpoint is secure and user inputs are properly sanitized. Always follow best practices when dealing with remote data sources.
']

