public class RemoteTaskExecutor {
    private final ExecutorService executor;
    private final JSch sshClient;
    private final List<Future> tasks = new ArrayList<>();

    public RemoteTaskExecutor(int maxConcurrentTasks, CloudProviderAPI cloudApi) {
        executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(maxConcurrentTasks);
        sshClient = new JSch();
    }

    public void executeCommandOnRemoteServer(String serverAddress, String command) {
        Future futureTask = executor.submit(() -> {
            try {
                Session session = sshClient.getSession("username", serverAddress);
                session.setPassword("password");

                // add retry logic here...
                while (true) {
                    try {
                        session.connect();
                        break;
                    } catch (JSchException e) {
                        // handle exception here...
                    }
                }

                ChannelExec channel = (ChannelExec) session.openChannel("exec");
                channel.setCommand(command);
                channel.connect();
                String output = IOUtils.toString(channel.getInputStream());

                // process command output here...
            } catch (JSchException | IOException e) {
                // handle exception here...
            } finally {
                // cleanup session and channel here...
            }
        });

        tasks.add(futureTask);
    }

    public void waitForAllTasksToComplete() throws InterruptedException, ExecutionException {
        for (Future task : tasks) {
            task.get();
        }
    }
}
```
This is a high level pseudo code and not a complete solution. You will need to fill in many details like SSH credentials handling, error handling, concurrent processing control, backpressure and queuing, circuit breaker pattern implementation, etc. It's recommended that you have a team with expert knowledge of Java and system design to tackle this task effectively. 

